    margin-top: 16px;
  }
  .methodology strong { color: var(--text-muted); }

  /* Footer */
  footer {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 24px;
    margin-top: 48px;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="page-wrapper">

  <!-- ═══════════════════ HEADER ═══════════════════ -->
  <header class="report-header">
    <div class="tag">Analytical Report · 2026 Edition</div>
    <h1>Active Satellites in Earth Orbit<br>2026 Catalog Analysis</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">A data-driven examination of 14,875 active spacecraft — orbital regime distribution, constellation composition, launch acceleration, and policy implications for space sustainability.</p>
    <div class="meta">
      <span><strong>Data Source:</strong> CelesTrak / NORAD TLE Catalog</span>
      <span><strong>Epoch Window:</strong> 2026-02-26 — 2026-03-30</span>
      <span><strong>Records Analyzed:</strong> 14,875</span>
      <span><strong>Audience:</strong> Space-Industry Analysts &amp; Policy Advisors</span>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- ═══════════════════ KPI BLOCK ═══════════════════ -->
  <div class="kpi-grid">
    <div class="kpi-card blue">
      <div class="kpi-label">Total Active Satellites</div>
      <div class="kpi-value blue">14,875</div>
      <div class="kpi-note">Full catalog as of Mar 2026</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card green">
      <div class="kpi-label">LEO Share</div>
      <div class="kpi-value green">86.45%</div>
      <div class="kpi-note">12,860 satellites · MEAN_MOTION &gt; 14</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card orange">
      <div class="kpi-label">Starlink Constellation</div>
      <div class="kpi-value orange">10,083</div>
      <div class="kpi-note">67.78% of all active satellites</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card purple">
      <div class="kpi-label">Median Inclination</div>
      <div class="kpi-value purple">53.16°</div>
      <div class="kpi-note">Reflects Starlink 53° shell dominance</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card red">
      <div class="kpi-label">Launched Since 2020</div>
      <div class="kpi-value red">13,461</div>
      <div class="kpi-note">90.5% of fleet · massive recent surge</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ═══════════════════ SECTION 1: CATALOG OVERVIEW ═══════════════════ -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-num">01</span>
      <h2>Catalog Overview &amp; Key Figures</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="section-divider"></div>

    <p>The CelesTrak/NORAD catalog snapshot (epoch window: Feb 26 – Mar 30, 2026) contains <strong>14,875 active, trackable spacecraft</strong>. This figure represents objects with valid TLE elements — payloads, not debris or rocket bodies. The catalog spans six decades of spaceflight, from CALSPHERE 1 (launched 1964) to satellites deployed weeks before the snapshot date.</p>

    <p>Orbit shapes are overwhelmingly circular: <strong>98.96% of satellites have eccentricity below 0.01</strong>, consistent with operational station-keeping requirements. Only 0.28% occupy highly elliptical orbits (eccentricity &gt; 0.1), a category historically used for wide-area coverage (Molniya) and now comparatively rare.</p>

    <div class="stat-row">
      <div class="stat-item"><div class="s-label">Near-Circular (ecc &lt; 0.01)</div><div class="s-val">98.96%</div></div>
      <div class="stat-item"><div class="s-label">Moderate Eccentricity</div><div class="s-val">0.76%</div></div>
      <div class="stat-item"><div class="s-label">Highly Elliptical (ecc &gt; 0.1)</div><div class="s-val">0.28%</div></div>
      <div class="stat-item"><div class="s-label">Mean Eccentricity</div><div class="s-val">0.00229</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="chart-grid-2">
      <div class="chart-card">
        <h3>Inclination Distribution (all satellites)</h3>
        <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="incDistChart" height="220"></canvas></div>
      </div>
      <div class="chart-card">
        <h3>Mean Motion Distribution (rev/day)</h3>
        <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="mmDistChart" height="220"></canvas></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="methodology" style="margin-top:16px;">
      <strong>Data quality note:</strong> ECCENTRICITY, BSTAR, and MEAN_MOTION_DOT are stored as string-encoded scientific notation (e.g., ".002524") and were parsed to float before analysis. MEAN_MOTION_DDOT and EPHEMERIS_TYPE are uniformly 0 and excluded from analysis.
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════════════ SECTION 2: ORBITAL REGIMES ═══════════════════ -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-num">02</span>
      <h2>Orbital Regime Classification</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="section-divider"></div>

    <p>Satellites are classified into four orbital regimes using <strong>MEAN_MOTION thresholds</strong> derived from the TLE data. These thresholds correspond to well-established altitude bands as follows:</p>

    <div class="methodology" style="margin-bottom:18px;">
      <strong>Classification thresholds (MEAN_MOTION, rev/day):</strong><br>
      &nbsp;· <strong>LEO</strong> (Low Earth Orbit, ~160–2,000 km): MEAN_MOTION <strong>&gt; 14.0</strong><br>
      &nbsp;· <strong>MEO</strong> (Medium Earth Orbit, ~2,000–35,786 km): 2.0 &lt; MEAN_MOTION ≤ 14.0<br>
      &nbsp;· <strong>GEO</strong> (Geostationary Orbit, ~35,786 km): 0.9 ≤ MEAN_MOTION ≤ 2.0<br>
      &nbsp;· <strong>HEO</strong> (Highly Elliptical Orbit): MEAN_MOTION &lt; 0.9
    </div>

    <div class="regime-badges">
      <div class="regime-badge badge-leo">
        <span class="r-val">12,860</span>
        <span class="r-pct">86.45%</span>
        <span class="r-label">LEO</span>
      </div>
      <div class="regime-badge badge-meo">
        <span class="r-val">1,336</span>
        <span class="r-pct">8.98%</span>
        <span class="r-label">MEO</span>
      </div>
      <div class="regime-badge badge-geo">
        <span class="r-val">668</span>
        <span class="r-pct">4.49%</span>
        <span class="r-label">GEO</span>
      </div>
      <div class="regime-badge badge-heo">
        <span class="r-val">11</span>
        <span class="r-pct">0.07%</span>
        <span class="r-label">HEO</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="chart-grid-2">
      <div class="chart-card">
        <h3>Regime Distribution (satellite count)</h3>
        <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="regimeDonutChart" height="260"></canvas></div>
      </div>
      <div class="chart-card">
        <h3>Regime Share (% of total fleet)</h3>
        <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="regimeBarChart" height="260"></canvas></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="callout" style="margin-top:18px;">
      <strong>Starlink effect on LEO share:</strong> Starlink's 10,083 satellites almost entirely populate LEO (MEAN_MOTION ≈ 15.1 rev/day, altitude ~550 km). Removing Starlink, LEO still commands a plurality but drops to roughly <strong>58% of the remaining fleet</strong> — still dominant but less overwhelming.
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════════════ SECTION 3: CONSTELLATION ANALYSIS ═══════════════════ -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-num">03</span>
      <h2>Major Constellation &amp; Operator Breakdown</h2>
